  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "block_id": "h1-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Protocol Surfaces",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Rig Relay exposes four protocol surfaces for different integration patterns. Each surface has a distinct role, transport, and authority model.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "ACP Agent \u2014 Editor \u2194 Agent",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Rig presents itself as a governed coding agent to editors and IDEs (Zed, JetBrains, VS Code). ACP standardizes session management, progress streaming, edit proposals, and permission gating.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "table-5",
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Concept",
        "Rig Mapping"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "ACP Session",
          "Rig mission / lane / worktree session"
        ],
        [
          "ACP Progress",
          "Rig progress events (phase, status, percent)"
        ],
        [
          "ACP Edit",
          "Rig patch proposal (never direct write)"
        ],
        [
          "ACP Permission",
          "Rig approval gate / authorization receipt"
        ],
        [
          "ACP Terminal",
          "Rig deterministic execution stream"
        ]
      ],
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "code-6",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "Editor/IDE  \u2192  ACP Client  \u2192  Rig ACP Agent\n  send session requests\n  receive plans, edits, progress\n  request permissions",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Entry point: `rig_relay.protocols.acp.RigACPAgent`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "MCP Client \u2014 Rig \u2194 External Tools",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Rig consumes external MCP servers for additional tools, databases, and context sources. Rig acts as an MCP host, connecting to servers over stdio or Streamable HTTP.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This surface is future work. The adapter layer is designed but not yet wired to the tool manager.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-11",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "MCP Server \u2014 Host \u2194 Rig Tools",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Rig exposes governed tools, resources, and prompts to MCP hosts (Antigravity, Claude Desktop, Cursor, Zed). Tools are tiered: read-only context first, mutation gated behind authorization receipts.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "code-13",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "Antigravity / Claude / Cursor / Zed\n  \u2192  MCP Client\n    \u2192  Rig MCP Server\n      \u2192  governed tool execution\n      \u2192  receipt-backed result",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Entry point: `rig_relay.protocols.mcp.RigMCPServer`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Transport: stdio (local) or Streamable HTTP (remote).",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-16",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Tool Tiers",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "table-17",
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Tier",
        "Access",
        "Examples"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "0 \u2014 Read-only",
          "Always available",
          "`rig.current_mission`, `rig.summarize_dirty_state`, `rig.list_worktrees`"
        ],
        [
          "1 \u2014 Analysis",
          "Always available",
          "`rig.build_context_packet`, `rig.create_consult_packet`"
        ],
        [
          "2 \u2014 Validation",
          "Always available",
          "`rig.run_validator`, `rig.check_merge_friendly`"
        ],
        [
          "3 \u2014 Patch proposal",
          "Gated",
          "`rig.propose_patch` \u2014 returns approval gate"
        ],
        [
          "4 \u2014 Mutation",
          "Requires auth receipt",
          "`rig.request_user_approval`"
        ],
        [
          "5 \u2014 Git/release",
          "Denied by default",
          "`rig.promote_to_preproduction`"
        ]
      ],
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-18",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Every Tier 3+ tool returns `blocked_pending_approval` + `receipt_id` + `approval_required: true`.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-19",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "WebSocket \u2014 Cockpit \u2194 Backend",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Local projection stream for the desktop cockpit. Token-gated, localhost-only (`127.0.0.1`), content-light. Clients authenticate with a session token, then subscribe to projection pushes, request chat state, send messages, and dispatch desktop intents.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "code-21",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "Frontend (pywebview)  \u2192  WebSocket  \u2192  ProjectionWebSocketServer\n  auth, subscribe, get_projection, send_chat_message, desktop_intent\n  \u2190  projection, chat_state, progress_events, intent_results",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-22",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Port: 9876 (default). Token auto-generated per session, delivered via inline script injection in the HTML payload.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    }
  ],
  "provenance": {
    "source_files": [
      "docs/protocol-surfaces.md"
    ]
  }
}
